<!-- ── FAQ ── -->
<section class="section">
  <p class="section-label">FAQ</p>
  <h2 class="section-title">Questions? Answers.</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need an account to send an invoice?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">Yes — your account keeps your invoices, clients, and settings private and secure. Sign-up takes about 30 seconds.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I use my own domain for invoice links?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">For now, invoice links use the JustInvoice domain. You can deploy JustInvoice on your own server with your own domain if you self-host — the codebase is self-contained.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What payment methods can clients use?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">Any card Stripe accepts — Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Discover, and more. ACH, bank transfers, and wallets depend on your Stripe account configuration.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I cancel anytime?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">Yes. Cancel whenever you like from your settings page. Your data stays accessible (exportable) even after cancellation.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is there a free trial?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">There's no trial period because the $9/month price is built to be affordable from day one — not a bait-and-switch. Start free, pay when you're earning.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What happens when my client pays?</summary>
      <p class="faq-answer">Stripe processes the card and deposits the money directly into your linked bank account. JustInvoice updates the invoice status to "Paid" automatically via webhook — no manual work required.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

